{"id":"rmse_distance","title":"Root mean square error","family":"lock-step","definition":"reference","intro_en":"RMSE averages squared residuals before taking a square root. For vectors of one fixed length it is Euclidean distance divided by the square root of that length. The animation separates the squared-error accumulation, averaging, and final root so its difference from a raw Euclidean total is visible.","intro_zh":"RMSE 先对平方误差取平均，再开平方。向量长度固定时，它等于欧氏距离除以长度的平方根。动图将平方累加、求平均和开平方分开，说明它与未归一化欧氏距离的关系。","steps_en":["Keep the two series on the same sample grid; no shift or warping is estimated.","Square each residual; the highlighted point supplies one coordinate contribution.","Accumulate the coordinate contributions in sample order.","Divide by sample count, then take the square root."],"steps_zh":["在同一采样网格上比较两条序列，不估计平移或时间规整。","计算各坐标残差的平方。","按采样顺序累积局部贡献。","平方差总和除以样本数后，再开平方。"],"formula":"sqrt(mean_i (x_i-y_i)^2)","caveats_en":["The fixed-length equivalence does not justify comparing different missing-data or alignment protocols.","Sample alignment and amplitude units are part of the comparison protocol."],"caveats_zh":["固定长度下的等价关系不能代替缺失值和对齐协议的一致性。","采样对齐和幅值单位属于比较协议的一部分。"],"sources":[{"label":"SciPy: euclidean","url":"https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.spatial.distance.euclidean.html"}],"x":[1.0,1.5,2.4,3.7,4.5,3.8,2.6,2.1,2.8,3.8,4.1,3.3],"y":[1.3,1.8,2.0,3.2,5.2,4.4,2.9,1.6,2.6,3.1,4.4,3.9],"input_label":"Deterministic synthetic illustration; sample index is the time axis.","parameters":{"samples":12,"preprocessing":"none","domain":"strictly positive illustration"},"result":{"label":"distance","value":0.479583152331272,"detail":"Exact formula evaluation on the displayed aligned vectors."},"frames":[{"phase":0,"caption":"Aligned samples","panel":{"kind":"lines","title":"Aligned samples","a":[1.0,1.5],"a_label":"x","b":[1.3,1.8],"b_label":"y","marker":1}},{"phase":0,"caption":"Aligned samples","panel":{"kind":"lines","title":"Aligned samples","a"